  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [removal steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#the-iframe-element:unload-a-document:~:text=The%20iframe%20HTML%20element%20removing%20steps%2C%20given%20removedNode%2C%20are%20to%20destroy%20a%20child%20navigable%20given%20removedNode%2E) for iframes destroy the child navigable. This never updates the content document's [visibility state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#visibility-state). That only happens when [unloading](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#unload-a-document) a document.\n\nAll major browsers (Firefox, Chromium, WebKit) set the iframe's document to hidden when it is removed:\n```js\nlet frame = document.createElement(\"iframe\");\ndocument.body.appendChild(frame);\nlet doc = frame.contentDocument;\nconsole.log(doc.visibilityState);\n\nframe.remove();\nconsole.log(doc.visibilityState);\n```",
